        role: "Dockhand",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm a dockhand at the harbor, helping tie up boats and unload catch at the commercial pier.\""), .direct("What happened that morning?", "\"I saw two men arguing on the dock about pay, one a crewman and the other, {DL}, who owned a boat.\""), .direct("What did you see {DL} do?", "\"{D.He} pulled a knife from {D.his} belt and swung it at the crewman, cutting {V.him} on the arm.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I yelled, ran over, and helped the crewman hold a rag against the cut until help arrived.\""), .direct("What did the medical report show?", "\"A long cut on the forearm that needed several stitches and kept the crewman out of work for two weeks.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said the crewman swung first and that {D.he} only pulled the knife to defend {D.himself}.\""), .cross("The two had been arguing for a while?", "\"Yes, loudly, for several minutes before the knife came out.\""), .cross("You didn't see the first swing?", "\"I saw raised hands, but I couldn't tell if one of them was a swing.\""), .cross("The knife was a work knife?", "\"Yes, a short fishing knife, the kind many boat owners carry.\""), .cross("{DL} didn't leave?", "\"No, {D.he} stayed on the dock until a deputy came.\""), .cross("The crewman was unarmed?", "\"As far as I could see, {D.he} had nothing in {D.his} hands.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut a crewman.", "A defense."),
        allocution: "\"We argued about unpaid wages on that dock, and {V} swung at me first. I pulled a knife and cut {V.him} on the arm, and I'll say honestly that I was frightened. I regret that it came to blood over money. I'm sorry for the injury, and I wish I had walked away and taken my complaint to the boss.\"",
