        openings: ("A dockhand tying up boats at the commercial pier saw two men argue about pay on the dock, a crewman and {D}, who owned a boat, and the crewman was cut on the arm, and the dockhand says '{D} had the knife.' {DL} came before this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say {V} swung first on the dock and {D} defended {D.himself} with what was in {D.his} hand. A man who is struck may strike back, and {D} did not follow {V}."),
