        spec: "Communicated a threat to {V} to cause fear, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, a pharmacy received a letter promising a shooting. Handwriting matched {D}. {DL} says it was a joke.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Letter", "'Friday you're shot.'"), E(.forensic, 2, "Handwriting Report", "Matches {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Joke", "{DL} says it was a joke.")],
        role: "Pharmacist",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm the pharmacist at a small pharmacy that fills prescriptions for many patients on dialysis.\""), .direct("What did you receive?", "\"A typed letter in the mail that said, 'Friday you're shot,' with no signature and no return address.\""), .direct("How did you take it?", "\"Very seriously. We closed the pharmacy for the afternoon and called the sheriff's office immediately.\""), .direct("What did the investigators find?", "\"A handwriting examiner compared the letter to samples and concluded that the writing matches {DL}'s.\""), .direct("What connection does {DL} have to the pharmacy?", "\"{DL} was a customer who was angry about a prescription that I refused to fill without a new authorization.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said it was a joke and that {D.he} never meant it as a real threat.\""), .cross("The letter doesn't say who would shoot you?", "\"No, it only says 'Friday you're shot,' with no name.\""), .cross("It could have been written by someone with a similar hand?", "\"The examiner said the match was strong, though she can't be absolutely certain.\""), .cross("Nothing happened on Friday?", "\"No, we had a deputy outside all day, and nothing occurred.\""), .cross("{DL} has a legitimate prescription issue?", "\"Yes, and we later filled it once the authorization came.\""), .cross("You had no other threats?", "\"None before or since this one.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threatened a pharmacy.", "A joke."),
        allocution: "\"I wrote that letter as a joke, and I never meant to scare anyone. I see now that a threat about a shooting is nothing to joke about, and I'm sorry for the fear it caused at the pharmacy. The staff should not have to open that kind of mail. I will never write anything like it again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a prior case in this court.", "{DL} apologized within the hour."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you write the letter?", "\"Yes. I was angry about the prescription, and I wrote it in a moment of bad judgment.\""), .direct("What did you mean by it?", "\"I meant it as a dark joke to show how angry I was. I never planned to hurt anyone.\""), .direct("Why did you pick a Friday?", "\"I don't know. It was just a day. I wasn't thinking of a plan or of any place.\""), .direct("Do you own a gun?", "\"I own a hunting rifle that's locked in a closet. I never took it out for any reason related to this.\""), .direct("What did you do after you mailed it?", "\"I regretted it right away, and I almost called to say I was sorry. I was ashamed.\""), .direct("What would you tell the pharmacist?", "\"I'm sorry for frightening you and your staff. I'll never send anything like that again.\""), .cross("You've been charged with threatening someone in writing before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and the court warned me about it. I let my anger get the better of me again.\""), .cross("A letter that says someone will be shot is a threat, isn't it?", "\"It is, whether I meant it or not, and I understand that now.\""), .cross("You wrote it by hand so it could be traced to you?", "\"I typed it, but the signature line was in my handwriting. I didn't try to hide.\""), .cross("You'll stay away from the pharmacy?", "\"Yes, and I'll use a different pharmacy in another town.\""), .cross("You'll accept counseling for your anger?", "\"Yes, and I'll go to every session.\"")],
        openings: ("A pharmacist at a small pharmacy that fills prescriptions for many dialysis patients received a typed letter in the mail that said 'Friday you're shot,' with no signature and no return address, and a handwriting report matches {D}, and {DL} had faced this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say it was a joke, a foolish letter meant to frighten no one. {D} never meant to hurt anyone."),
        closings: ("The letter promises a shooting on a Friday, the handwriting report matches {D}, and after {PRIOR} {DL} knew exactly how those words would be read.", "A joke is not a threat unless it is meant as one, and {D} never came near the pharmacy. The State must prove {D} meant the pharmacist to fear harm when {D.he} wrote the letter."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 a.m.: letter."), (1, "Arrest.")],
        identified: "Handwriting.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a threat"],
        mood: .divided,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let lotWrenchAgain = SmallCases.make(
